    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key per the spec. The project uses OfficeFloor function pipelines (not Spring MVC controllers), so all logic lives in small function classes.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 standard American (Russell/NARA) Soundex encoder for surnames, so names that sound alike share a code (e.g. `Smith`/`Smyth` \u2192 `S530`).\n\n2. **`OwnerIdentityKey.java`** \u2014 the key is now the **lower-case hex SHA-256** (64 chars) over `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + lowerEmail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)`, replacing the old plain-string form that used `householdId`. Both `forRequest` and `forOwner` now feed `lastName` through Soundex.\n\n3. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 the soft-match trigger changed from *(exact lastName + postcode + different telephone)* to *(**soundex(lastName)** equal + postcode equal + **identityKey differs**)*, still ignoring soft-deleted owners and picking the lowest matching id.\n\n4. **`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java`** \u2014 docs updated to reflect the single identity-key check; the code already delegates to `OwnerIdentityKey`, so it now uses the hashed key, still ignores deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in `ValidateNewOwner` (a 400 before this step).\n\n**Spec conformance:**\n- identityKey = SHA-256 hex over the three normalized components \u2713\n- 409 duplicate detection uses the key, ignoring deleted owners, blocklist applied first \u2713\n- soft-match now fires when the key differs but soundex(lastName) + postcode match \u2713\n- same lastName + postcode but different telephone \u2192 soft match, not 409 (different phone \u2192 different key) \u2713\n- postcode/householdId no longer contributes to the hard-duplicate key, so the separate household-duplicate 409 block no longer applies \u2713\n\n**Test results:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (collision \u2192 409) both green; full `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nOne note: `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` retains the `sharesHousehold` bypass (an explicit caller hint, orthogonal to the key redesign) \u2014 a legitimate second household member already gets a distinct key via their different telephone, so this only affects the untested edge case of an exact-identity resubmission that self-declares `sharesHousehold`. I left it in place to avoid changing undocumented, untested behavior; let me know if you'd prefer the key to be the sole arbiter with no bypass.",
